/**
 * @defgroup optimal_specific_speed_correction_calculator Specific Speed Efficiency Correction
 * @ingroup equipment_and_property_calculators
 * @brief HI 20.3-2020 efficiency decrement from US customary specific speed.
 * @details
 * How much should the base pump efficiency decrease for this specific speed? The result is a
 * dimensionless fraction to subtract from the viscosity-adjusted efficiency, not a multiplier.
 *
 * @heading{Result and Decision Path}
 * HI correction data are percentage points. Interpolate in specific speed, then divide by 100.
 * Only vertical turbine uses V; axial flow and all other classifications use All but V.
 *
 * @formula{hi2020-speed-correction;
 * C_{Ns}=\frac{\operatorname{PCHIP}_{category}(N_s)}{100}
 * }
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{C_{Ns}; Fractional efficiency decrement to subtract; \unitless}
 * @symrow{N_s; US customary specific speed; rpm sqrt(US gpm)/ft^(3/4)}
 * @symrow{category; V or All but V table selection; \unitless}
 * @symrow{100; Percentage-point scale per fraction; \percent}
 * @endsymtable
 *
 * Specific speed itself remains defined in @ref optimal_specific_speed_calculator. Total head is
 * divided by stage count in that calculation. This correction neither recomputes specific speed
 * nor halves flow for double suction.
 *
 * | Category | Inclusive specific-speed range (US convention) |
 * | --- | --- |
 * | V | 1717.2–17172 |
 * | All but V | 630–6300 |
 *
 * The V data include a zero plateau from 4293 to 5151.6. Shape-preserving interpolation keeps
 * the plateau zero and avoids negative overshoot around the minimum. The nonvertical minimum
 * is zero at 2160. No polynomial extension or extrapolation is used.
 *
 * @heading{Worked Example}
 * For a nonvertical pump at Ns=990 in the US convention, PCHIP returns approximately 6.595
 * percentage points. The returned correction is approximately 0.06595. For an efficiency fraction
 * of 0.8 before this correction, the adjusted efficiency would therefore be about 0.73405 (73.405%).
 * Subtracting 6.595 directly from a fractional efficiency would mix units.
 *
 * @heading{Provenance and Availability}
 * Data follow the engineering PCHIP developer reference revised 2026-09-23 and HI 20.3-2020.
 * Endpoints are included. Nonfinite and out-of-range specific speeds return NaN, which means
 * no supported estimate, not zero correction. This limit applies to estimation; it does not make
 * a measured or supplied-efficiency assessment invalid. See @ref pchip_interpolation for tangents.
 *
 * @see optimal_specific_speed_correction::calculate
 */
